  <section>
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2>1. Dirac → Foldy–Wouthuysen Fine Structure &amp; Helium Ritz Bracket</h2>
      <span class="mod-tag">chem/fineclaim.cub · chem/witnessclaim.cub · chem/sylvester.cub</span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-head">
          <span>Interactive Hydrogen Fine-Structure Spectrum (n ≤ 6)</span>
          <span id="fsInfo">n = 3 · exact (Zα)² splitting</span>
        </div>
        <canvas id="fsCanvas"></canvas>
        <div class="ctrl">
          <label>Principal n <input type="range" id="fsN" min="1" max="6" value="3"><span id="fsNVal">n = 3</span></label>
          <label>Coupling Zα <input type="range" id="fsZa" min="1" max="45" value="22"><span id="fsZaVal">0.22</span></label>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="thm"><b>fine-to-n6 : fn-all-ok 6 ≡ true</b> — For every \(n \le 6\), \(l &lt; n\), and \(j = l \pm \frac{1}{2}\), Dirac's exact level expanded in \(x = (Z\alpha)^2\) matches Schrödinger \(-1/(2n^2)\) plus Foldy–Wouthuysen's \(p^4\), Darwin, and spin-orbit sum \(-\frac{1}{2n^4}(\frac{n}{\kappa} - \frac{3}{4})\).</div>
        <p><b>Helium ground energy (`chem/witnessclaim.cub`):</b> On the 7-function Hylleraas basis at \(\alpha = 7/4\), Bareiss integer elimination + Sylvester inertia soundness (<code>inertia-cert-sound</code>) certifies the lowest Ritz level in \([-3044409, -3044408]/2^{20} = [-2.9033747, -2.9033737]\) Ha with zero floating-point arithmetic.</p>
        <pre>he7-wit : wt-bracket (he-prob 7 4 he-b7) 0 (hc-negk 3044 409)
                     (hc-negk 3044 408) (true , bin-pow2 20) ≡ true
fc-car  : fq-eq (fq-add (fq-mul (fa-an 0) (fa-cr 0)) (fq-e 0 0)) fq-one ≡ true</pre>
      </div>
    </div>
