  <section>
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2>2. Bioelectric Gap-Junction Coupling &amp; Isopotential Domain Collapse</h2>
      <span class="mod-tag">chem/basin-compose.cub · neuro/barrier.cub (bioelectric-gap-split-sos-id)</span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-head">
          <span>Two-Cell Bioelectric Domain (Levin Cognitive Light Cone)</span>
          <span id="bioInfo">g_c = 2.0 · ISOPOTENTIAL MERGE</span>
        </div>
        <canvas id="bioCanvas"></canvas>
        <div class="ctrl">
          <label>Gap junction g_c <input type="range" id="bioGc" min="0" max="60" value="20"><span id="bioGcVal">2.0</span></label>
          <label>Leak g <input type="range" id="bioG" min="2" max="20" value="6"><span id="bioGVal">0.6</span></label>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="thm"><b>bioelectric-gap-split-sos-id</b> — Exact orthogonal decomposition of two-cell bioelectric dissipation:
        $$2\bigl(g(V_1-E)^2 + g(V_2-E)^2 + g_c(V_1-V_2)^2\bigr) = g(V_1+V_2-2E)^2 + (g+2g_c)(V_1-V_2)^2$$</div>
        <p>Drag \(g_c \to 0\) (gap-junction blocker / cancer decoupling): the difference mode \(V_1 - V_2\) decouples and each cell collapses to its own isolated local basin. Increase \(g_c\): the difference mode damps at rate \(g + 2g_c\), collapsing the pair onto the collective isopotential quotient \(V_1 = V_2\) (<code>basin-couple-merges</code> in <code>chem/basin-compose.cub</code>).</p>
